        { id: "s14", label: "Related Standards" },
        { id: "s15", label: "Glossary" }
      ]}
    />
  </Fragment>
  <div class="wrap">



<div class="section-header" id="s1"><span class="num">1</span><h2>Conceptual Framework Linkage</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Accounting for the pension vehicle, not the sponsoring employer</div><div class="principle">ASBE No. 10 governs the RECOGNITION, MEASUREMENT, and PRESENTATION of financial STATEMENTS for an "ENTERPRISE ANNUITY FUND" (企业年金基金) — a VOLUNTARY, SUPPLEMENTARY occupational PENSION vehicle Chinese ENTERPRISES may ESTABLISH in ADDITION to the MANDATORY state BASIC pension INSURANCE system (see the COMPANION ASBE No. 9 poster). GENUINELY DISTINCTIVELY, this Standard addresses the FUND'S OWN separate ACCOUNTING — NOT the sponsoring EMPLOYER'S contribution EXPENSE, which is SIMPLY treated as an ORDINARY employee BENEFIT cost under ASBE No. 9.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s2"><span class="num">2</span><h2>Scope — the Fund's Own Financial Statements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A dedicated reporting entity, separate from the employer</div><div class="principle">This Standard applies to the ENTERPRISE ANNUITY FUND ITSELF — a SEGREGATED, TRUSTEE-managed POOL of assets HELD for the BENEFIT of PARTICIPATING employees — REQUIRING its OWN set of FINANCIAL statements, DISTINCT from BOTH the SPONSORING employer's statements AND the INDIVIDUAL participating EMPLOYEE'S own position.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s3"><span class="num">3</span><h2>What an Enterprise Annuity Is</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A voluntary "third pillar" supplement to the mandatory state pension</div><div class="text-supporting">An "ENTERPRISE ANNUITY" is a VOLUNTARY OCCUPATIONAL pension ARRANGEMENT some Chinese ENTERPRISES establish to SUPPLEMENT the MANDATORY state BASIC pension SYSTEM — BROADLY analogous to a "THIRD PILLAR" or SUPPLEMENTARY workplace PENSION scheme INTERNATIONALLY, FUNDED through JOINT employer/employee CONTRIBUTIONS, MANAGED by INDEPENDENT trustees or FUND managers on the PARTICIPANTS' behalf.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s4"><span class="num">4</span><h2>Distinguishing This Standard From ASBE No. 9</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Two entirely different accounting questions</div><div class="text-supporting">ASBE No. 9 addresses HOW the SPONSORING employer ACCOUNTS for its OWN contribution EXPENSE (a STRAIGHTFORWARD periodic COST, much like the STATE pension SYSTEM'S own treatment). ASBE No. 10, BY CONTRAST, addresses an ENTIRELY DIFFERENT question: HOW the FUND ITSELF — as a SEPARATE reporting ENTITY holding and INVESTING the POOLED contributions — RECOGNISES and MEASURES its OWN assets, LIABILITIES, and NET assets AVAILABLE for BENEFITS.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s5"><span class="num">5</span><h2>Measurement of Fund Assets — Fair Value Throughout</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Financial assets measured at fair value, with changes in profit or loss</div><div class="text-supporting">FINANCIAL assets OBTAINED by an ENTERPRISE annuity FUND are MEASURED at FAIR VALUE, with CHANGES between the CARRYING amount and the FAIR value RECOGNISED in PROFIT or LOSS — a GENUINELY notable EXCEPTION to the GENERAL cost-model CAUTION seen ELSEWHERE across the ASBE asset STANDARDS (Fixed Assets, INVESTMENT Property, BIOLOGICAL Assets — see the COMPANION posters), REFLECTING the FUND'S fundamentally INVESTMENT-oriented purpose.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s6"><span class="num">6</span><h2>The Fund's Financial Statements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">A statement of net assets available for benefits</div><div class="text-supporting">The FUND prepares its OWN financial STATEMENTS — PRINCIPALLY a STATEMENT of NET assets AVAILABLE for BENEFITS, and a STATEMENT of CHANGES in NET assets AVAILABLE for BENEFITS — SHOWING contributions RECEIVED, investment INCOME earned, benefit PAYMENTS made, and the FUND'S overall NET asset POSITION, WITHOUT attempting to VALUE the participants' INDIVIDUAL accrued PENSION entitlements (a SEPARATE actuarial QUESTION beyond this Standard's SCOPE).</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s7"><span class="num">7</span><h2>A Genuinely Rare Standard-Level Treatment Internationally</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">A dedicated standard for a topic IFRS addresses only narrowly</div><div class="text-supporting">INTERNATIONALLY, IAS 26 (ACCOUNTING and REPORTING by RETIREMENT BENEFIT Plans) addresses a BROADLY SIMILAR topic — the FINANCIAL statements of the RETIREMENT benefit PLAN itself, RATHER than the SPONSORING employer — but IS considerably LESS prominently EMPHASISED or WIDELY applied in PRACTICE than ASBE No. 10 is WITHIN China's OWN standard-setting LANDSCAPE, GIVEN the GROWING significance of ENTERPRISE annuity SCHEMES as a SUPPLEMENTARY pension VEHICLE.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s8"><span class="num">8</span><h2>Worked Example — Measuring Fund Financial Assets at Fair Value</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cw span2"><div class="ctitle cw">Recognising investment gains directly in the fund's own results</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: A fund's bond portfolio</div><div class="wk-body">An enterprise annuity fund holds a bond portfolio with a carrying amount of RMB 200,000,000. At the reporting date, the portfolio's fair value has risen to RMB 208,000,000.</div><div class="wk-answer">The fund recognises the ASSETS at their FAIR value of RMB 208,000,000, with the RMB 8,000,000 INCREASE recognised WITHIN the fund's OWN statement of CHANGES in net ASSETS available for BENEFITS — REFLECTING the FUND'S OWN investment PERFORMANCE, ENTIRELY separate from the SPONSORING employer's own FINANCIAL statements.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s9"><span class="num">9</span><h2>Worked Example — Contrasting the Employer's and the Fund's Own Accounting</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Two separate sets of books for the same underlying arrangement</div>
<div class="worked" style="margin-bottom:0;"><div class="wk-title">Example: An employer's contribution to its own annuity fund</div><div class="wk-body">A company contributes RMB 5,000,000 during the year to its own enterprise annuity fund.</div><div class="wk-answer">The COMPANY (the EMPLOYER) simply RECOGNISES an EXPENSE of RMB 5,000,000 under ASBE No. 9, MUCH like an ORDINARY employee benefit COST. The FUND, SEPARATELY, recognises the SAME RMB 5,000,000 as a CONTRIBUTION RECEIVED WITHIN its OWN statement of CHANGES in net ASSETS, under ASBE No. 10 — TWO entirely DIFFERENT sets of ACCOUNTING for the SAME underlying CASH movement.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s10"><span class="num">10</span><h2>Disclosure Requirements</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">What ASBE No. 10 requires</div><div class="check-list"><span>Net assets available for benefits, and changes therein during the period</span><span>Fair value measurement basis for the fund's financial assets</span><span>Contributions received and benefit payments made during the period</span></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s11"><span class="num">11</span><h2>Critical Judgments &amp; Estimates</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2"><div class="ctitle cn">Where judgement matters most</div>
<div class="two-col"><div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT JUDGEMENTS</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Correctly distinguishing the fund's own accounting from the sponsoring employer's accounting for the same arrangement</span></div></div>
<div><div class="elabel">SIGNIFICANT ESTIMATES</div><div class="dot-list"><span>Fair value of the fund's investment portfolio</span></div></div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s12"><span class="num">12</span><h2>Relationship to IAS 26</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card ci span2"><div class="ctitle ci">Comparison — ASBE 10 vs IAS 26</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Feature</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-warning);">ASBE 10</span><span style="color:var(--color-text-info);">IAS 26</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Subject matter</span><span>Reporting by the retirement benefit vehicle itself</span><span>Reporting by the retirement benefit plan itself — converged in objective</span></div>
<div class="tr alt" style="grid-template-columns:1.2fr 1.2fr 1.2fr;"><span>Measurement of fund investments</span><span>Fair value, changes to profit or loss</span><span>Fair value — converged</span></div>
</div>
<div class="note">A GENUINELY rare CASE where China has a MORE prominently applied, DEDICATED standard for a TOPIC that INTERNATIONALLY receives RELATIVELY narrow, LESS frequently applied TREATMENT under IAS 26.</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s13"><span class="num">13</span><h2>Statement Mapping</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cs span2"><div class="ctitle cs">Where every enterprise annuity fund event lands (within the fund's own statements)</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Event</span><span>Statement(s) affected</span><span>Notes</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:1.6fr 1fr 1.4fr;"><span>Fair value change in fund investments</span><span>Fund's own statement of changes in net assets</span><span>Not reflected in the sponsoring employer's own financial statements</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s14"><span class="num">14</span><h2>Related Standards</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cd span2"><div class="ctitle cd">Cross-reference map</div>
<div class="td-table"><div class="th" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>Standard</span><span>Connection</span></div>
<div class="tr" style="grid-template-columns:0.8fr 2fr;"><span>ASBE No. 9</span><span>Employee Benefits — governs the sponsoring employer's own contribution expense, distinct from this Standard's fund-level accounting</span></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="section-header" id="s15"><span class="num">15</span><h2>Quick-Reference Glossary</h2><span class="line"></span></div>
<div class="grid">
<div class="card cn span2">
<div class="glossary-item"><div class="glossary-term">Enterprise annuity (企业年金)</div><div class="glossary-def">A voluntary, supplementary occupational pension arrangement Chinese enterprises may establish in addition to the mandatory state basic pension system.</div></div>
<div class="glossary-item" style="border-bottom:none;"><div class="glossary-term">Net assets available for benefits</div><div class="glossary-def">The fund's own measure of its total assets less liabilities, representing the pool available to meet future participant benefit payments.</div></div>
</div>
</div>

<div class="legend"><div class="ltitle">Financial statement key (Chinese GAAP / ASBE terminology)</div><div class="lrow"><div class="litem"><span class="badge bs">BS</span> Balance Sheet (资产负债表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bp">IS</span> Income Statement (利润表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge be">SCOE</span> Statement of Changes in Owners' Equity (所有者权益变动表) </div><div class="litem"><span class="badge bc">CFS</span> Cash Flow Statement (现金流量表)</div></div></div>


</div>
  <section id="history">
    <HistoryTimeline items={history.asbe10 || []} />
  </section>
</StandardPageLayout>
